title: Climate Transition on track!
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: climate_transition_matures_trigger
max-visits: 1
role: event
on-arrival: {!
    G.deactivateLaw(Q, "climate_transition_core_initial", "expired");
    G.deactivateLaw(Q, "climate_binding_targets_initial", "expired");
    // TODO: Check that these become invisible indeed
    G.registerLaw(Q, {id:"climate_transition_core_mature",title:"Mature Climate Transition",icon:"img/leaf_icon.svg",targets:{gdp_growth:0.01,generalitat_surplus:-0.01,unemployment_recovery:0.015,welfare_index_growth:0.04}});
    if (!Q.climate_transition_contested_struck) {
        G.registerLaw(Q, {id:"climate_binding_targets_mature",title:"Binding Economy-Wide Climate Targets",icon:"img/leaf_icon.svg",targets:{gdp_growth:0.02,generalitat_surplus:-0.01,unemployment_recovery:0.005,welfare_index_growth:0.02}});
    }
    // TODO: Other conditions for this to trigger? not only passing the law right?
!}

= Climate Transition on track!

After the initial phases of sanctions, heavy investment and divestment, and arduous work, it seems that we're starting to see its first fruits. New industrial investment is already following the new regulations, and we're gradually seeing a moving away from the most polluting practices. The road ahead is still complex and this is far from addressing all the issues related to climate change, but it is definitely a start!

- @post_event: Great!
